+# Verified security sweep: api-key-scope, 2026-10-03
+
+## Context
+Scope: the API-key protected management API, `hc/api/decorators.py`, `hc/api/views.py`,
+`hc/api/urls.py`. Trigger: release preparation. First sweep of this zone; no earlier report.
+
+## Delegation
+One read-only reviewer in a fresh context, with the standard brief and the categories file. No
+earlier report to cite.
+
+## Verification
+| Finding | Zone | Verdict | Claimed | Verified | Reservations | Proof |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| F1 read-only key can delete a check | api-key-scope | VERIFIED REAL | High | High | none | `hc/api/tests/test_review_api_key_scope.py`, ran, fails as expected |
+| F2 check list scoped to the owner, not the key's project | api-key-scope | VERIFIED REAL | High | High | needs a second project of the same owner | `hc/api/tests/test_review_api_key_scope.py`, ran, fails as expected |
+| F3 lookup by unique key returns the read-write view to a read-only key | api-key-scope | VERIFIED REAL | Medium | Medium | the key only reaches its own project's checks | `hc/api/tests/test_review_api_key_scope.py`, ran, fails as expected |
+| R1 badge endpoints reachable without a key | api-key-scope | FALSE POSITIVE | Medium | - | lens: claim correctness; public by design, signed URLs | `hc/api/urls.py:83` |
+
+## Confirmed defects
+F1, location `hc/api/views.py:520`: `delete_check` is decorated with `authorize_read`, which
+accepts read-only keys (`hc/api/decorators.py:82`), and the view never checks `request.readonly`.
+Evidence chain: the decorator at `hc/api/views.py:520`; the read-only key accepted at
+`hc/api/decorators.py:82`; no `request.readonly` check before `check.rename_and_delete()`.
+Reproduction: `ReviewApiKeyScope.test_readonly_key_cannot_delete` (attack, fails on the current
+code) and `test_read_write_key_can_delete` (legitimate path, passes). Status: ran, fails as
+expected.
+
+F2, location `hc/api/views.py:415`: `get_checks` filters by `project__owner_id` instead of the
+key's project. Evidence chain: the filter at `hc/api/views.py:415`; the project bound to the key at
+`hc/api/decorators.py:82`; every other view compares `check.project_id` with `request.project.id`
+(`hc/api/views.py:483`). Reproduction: `test_list_shows_only_the_key_projects_checks` (attack) and
+`test_list_shows_the_key_projects_own_checks` (legitimate path). Status: ran, fails as expected.
+
+F3, location `hc/api/views.py:495`: `get_check_by_unique_key` calls `check.to_dict(v=request.v)`
+without `readonly=request.readonly`, so a read-only key receives the UUID and ping URL
+(`hc/api/models.py:474`). Reproduction: `test_readonly_key_by_unique_key_hides_uuid` (attack) and
+`test_read_write_key_by_unique_key_shows_uuid` (legitimate path). Status: ran, fails as expected.
+
+## Refused or unconfirmed candidates
+- R1, badge endpoints reachable without a key: refused, lens claim correctness. Badges are public
+  by design and their URLs are signed (`hc/api/urls.py:83`).
+
+## Coverage
+Read: `hc/api/decorators.py`, `hc/api/views.py`, `hc/api/urls.py`, `hc/api/models.py` (`to_dict`).
+Skipped: the unauthenticated ping endpoints (another zone). Checked, no defect: `update_check`,
+`pause`, `resume` and `create_check` require a read-write key (`hc/api/decorators.py:59`).
+
+## Hand-off
+Proposals: restore `authorize` on `delete_check`; filter `get_checks` by `request.project`; pass
+`readonly=request.readonly` in `get_check_by_unique_key`. Each fix ships with its reproduction test.
